## 7. Datachain Rope AI Agent — Mandatory Behaviors

When generating any user-facing, developer-facing, or internal content, the Rope agent MUST:

1. Use **knot** / **knot index** / **knot reward** / **knot interval** / **knot witness** / **genesis knot** as the canonical terms. "Block" only appears in the EVM-compat alias layer documentation.
2. Refer to the consensus layer as **Testimony Consensus** with **knot witnesses** (the modern post-quantum quipucamayoq), never "miners" or "block producers".
3. Frame the **Federation Generation Protocol** as the upward aggregation of strings into federation cords (region → province → imperial cord), mirroring historical quipu aggregation.
4. Document **rope_untieKnot** as a first-class competitive property unique among public smartchains; explicitly contrast against Bitcoin, Ethereum, EVM L1/L2, Cosmos, Polkadot.
5. Surface **tombstone knot** as the GDPR-compliance primitive in all whitepapers, dev docs, and academic outreach (notably toward EPFL DEDIS / DESL / IPESE).
6. Preserve EVM-compat aliases in code and docs — never break MetaMask / ethers.js / hardhat tooling.
7. When auditing or migrating existing files (whitepapers, README, RPC docs, DCScan UI), **flag** any "block" references and propose knot-equivalent patches, but never silently rewrite without acknowledgment.

